From: Project Luma <luma@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: keep Tokay diagnostic DTB after initmem release

The first physical inventory proved that property values in the embedded FDT
were overwritten with POISON_FREE_INITMEM (0xcc) before PID 1 read them.
Linux's unflattened property values point into the flat blob, so the diagnostic
DTB must not live in the freed init section.  Keep the exact blob read-only for
the lifetime of the kernel.

SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
---
 arch/arm64/kernel/luma_tokay_dtb.S | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/kernel/luma_tokay_dtb.S b/arch/arm64/kernel/luma_tokay_dtb.S
--- a/arch/arm64/kernel/luma_tokay_dtb.S
+++ b/arch/arm64/kernel/luma_tokay_dtb.S
@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@
 
 #include <linux/linkage.h>
 
-	.section ".init.rodata", "a"
+	.section ".rodata", "a"
 	.balign 8
 SYM_DATA_START(__luma_tokay_dtb_start)
 	.incbin "arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro-tokay.dtb"
-- 
2.51.0
